      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Plants like Sansevieria do offer some acoustic dampening due to their fibrous leaves, but they cannot function as a native microphone array to track voices from a distance. The specific semi-circle and clustering patterns you observed are almost certainly intentional landscaping arrangements for visual appeal and plant health, not engineered sound collection systems. While they might slightly muffle direct noise, their structure lacks the necessary sensitivity and amplification to actively \"pick up\" ambient conversation from study carrels.",
